From: VKing <noreply@openwrt.local>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 16:03:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: classify VLAN zero as priority tagged

PPE classifies an 802.1Q header carrying VID 0 as priority tagged rather
than ordinarily tagged. Programming an explicit VLAN 0 ingress translation
rule with the tagged-only format therefore misses the packet.

Select the priority-tagged format only for explicit VID 0 rules. Preserve
the existing tagged match for non-zero VIDs and the combined untagged plus
priority-tagged match for PVID rules.

Signed-off-by: VKing <noreply@openwrt.local>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_config.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_config.c
@@ -1773,9 +1773,9 @@
 	rule[0] |= FIELD_PREP(PPE_XLT_RULE_W0_SKEY_FMT, PPE_XLT_FMT_UNTAGGED);

 	if (vid >= 0) {
-		fmt = PPE_XLT_FMT_TAGGED;
+		fmt = vid ? PPE_XLT_FMT_TAGGED : PPE_XLT_FMT_PRIO_TAGGED;
 		rule[1] |= PPE_XLT_RULE_W1_CKEY_VID_INCL;
 		rule[1] |= FIELD_PREP(PPE_XLT_RULE_W1_CKEY_VID, vid);
 	} else {
 		fmt = PPE_XLT_FMT_UNTAGGED | PPE_XLT_FMT_PRIO_TAGGED;
 	}
